instructions:
1. Cook the eggs sunny side up.
2. Cook the hamburger to your preference.
3. Steam the rice, and heat up the gravy.
4. Assemble the components in the following order:
5. * Rice on bottom;
6. * Hamburger on top of rice;
7. * Eggs;
8. * Gravy.

1. Crack the eggs into the mixing bowl, and beat them to homogenize.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 01.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 02.jpg|width=150|align=center}}
2. Mix in the sugar until well-distributed.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 03.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 04.jpg|width=150|align=center}}
3. Mix in the oil, then the milk.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 05.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 06.jpg|width=150|align=center}}
4. Sift in the flour, and mix just until incorporated.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 08.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 09.jpg|width=150|align=center|image3=Making sponge cake at home 10.jpg}}
5. Mix in the yeast powder.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 11.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 12.jpg|width=150|align=center}}
6. Transfer the batter to a cake pan lined with baking paper. Place the cake pan into the larger baking tray, and place them into the oven.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 13.jpg|image2=|width=150|align=center}}
7. Pour the hot water into the larger baking tray to make a water bath about 1–2 cm deep.
8. Set the oven to 150°C, and bake for 65 minutes or until a skewer inserted into the center comes out with no batter on it.
9. Remove the cake pan, and let it cool.
10. Unmold the cake, and cut into squares.{{Multiple image|image1=Making sponge cake at home 15.jpg|image2=Making sponge cake at home 16.jpg|width=200|align=center}}
